<title>UK: ICCO details result of cocoa buffer stock sale.</title>
<headline>ICCO details result of cocoa buffer stock sale.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Cocoa Organization (ICCO) said the 4,250 tonne buffer-stock sale earlier on Tuesday was completed at the following prices.</p>
<p> ORIGIN	TONNES   CROP YEAR  QUALITY    PORT     PRICE/TONNE</p>
<p>Cameroon	 25	1981/82     FF	Amsterdam    $1,201 </p>
<p>Cameroon	100	1982/83     GF	Amsterdam    $1,201 </p>
<p>Cote d'Ivoire  20	1979/80     GF	Amsterdam    $1,285 </p>
<p>Cote d'Ivoire 351	1982/83     GF	Amsterdam    $1,333-1,341 </p>
<p>Cote d'Ivoire 248	1982/83     FF	Amsterdam    $1,270 </p>
<p>Cote d'Ivoire 200	1983/84     GF	Amsterdam    $1,325-1,333 </p>
<p>Ghana	 1,244	1987/88     GF	 Hull	  $1,392-1,397 </p>
<p>Nigeria	  49	1986/87     GF	Amsterdam    $1,330 </p>
<p>Nigeria	  99	1986/87     FF	Amsterdam    $1,245 </p>
<p>Nigeria	 457	1986/87     GF	 Hull	  $1,309-1,325 </p>
<p>Nigeria</p>
<p>(GF=good fermented, FF=fair fermented, FAQ=fair to average quality)</p>
<p>The ICCO said the carry for forward delivery was calculated at $12 per tonne per month.</p>
<p>--Clelia Oziel, London Newsroom 44 171 542 8072.</p>
</text>
